A||N||5||Vlad||Car Bra||||1||
Z||000000||Vlad||02-05-2001||08:24 PM||||Hello guys,<P>I've been thinking about buying a front bra for my 85 GT. <BR>Any prons or cons?<BR>How difficult is to mount it? I assume very easy, but is there any drilling required?<BR>Also, what brand is the best?<P>Thanks<P>And please post pictures if possible.||||reg||1
Z||000001||KissMySSFiero||02-05-2001||10:37 PM||||i went with lebra. nice tight fit.  it was about 60 bucks from autozone. i got it to cover some front end damage so im not worried about damaging the finish.  no pics yet.  i have a coupe not a gt front though.  no drilling whatsoever on mine.  just loosen some screws and insert some metal tabs that came with the bra.  took about 20 min to install on a cool day.  supposed to do it when the weather is above 60 or so.  i like it because if i decide to get rid of it all i have to do is remove some velcro and a few tabs. here's one of another coupe with a lebra.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/adams-car.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:KissMySSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:KissMySSFiero@netzero.net">KissMySSFiero@netzero.net</A>   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">       <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"<BR><A HREF="http://expage.com/kissmyssfiero" TARGET=_blank>KissMySSFiero.mywebsite.hehe</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||02-06-2001||04:03 AM||||My 2  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/penny_spin_md_clr.gif"> <P><BR>LeBra is the best looking and fitting out there.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>WS6 Fieros "Members Photo Page"</A>||||reg||7
Z||000003||fierojunky||02-06-2001||08:50 AM||||I would advise buying a bra with the intention of leaving it on all the time.  My 87 SE had a bra on it when i bought it and i took it off to wash the car and have some bad fading.  Also I don't know if this is solely from the bra or not but the hood is crackling up on the two corners.  Anyways i but it back on just to hide the color being off.  Mines a LeBra and i think it looks the best too!||||reg||13
Z||000004||stsmithgt||02-06-2001||10:32 AM||||That AutoZone one looks good.  You still have  access to your trunk.  My Colgan one,  $80.00, is nice, but a hassle with the headlights.  I've had to pull over to roll up the covers on them. *pain when it's cold and raining*.  It's not too bad getting in the trunk.  I pull out the top two that are on a bungie and  FORCE the hood up. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I slide my knife in between the fender well and fender to shoehorn the hooks back in.  If I saw that AutoZone one, I would have bought that....||||reg||1
